<title>SPAIN: Spain reinstates 168 bln pta social security loan.</title>
<headline>Spain reinstates 168 bln pta social security loan.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government said on Friday it has reinstated a 167.84 billion peseta loan to the Social Security in order to cover a shortfall in the department's accounts.</p>
<p>A loan conceded by the previous Socialist government had been reduced by this amount, the government said in a note.</p>
</text>
